            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Clinical pharmacology is an essential discipline in the development of new medicines, but the closely specified requirements of pharmaceutical industry protocols and regulatory reviewers have limited the opportunities for curiosity-driven research. Realization is growing that there is so much that is not known about the mechanisms underlying human disease and the actions of medicines on them that research of a more exploratory kind, namely, investigative clinical pharmacology, is a priority.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
